    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Polynesian society on remote <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/easter-island">Easter Island</a>, settled around 1200 and organised in kin groups under a sacred paramount chief of the Miru clan.</li><li>Its people carved some 887 moai, mostly from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rano-raraku">Rano Raraku</a> tuff, and devised rongorongo, the only possible script known from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polynesia">Polynesia</a>.</li><li>Slave raids and epidemics in the 1860s reduced the islanders to 111 by 1877, and Chile annexed the island in 1888.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In the birdman rite, men swam to the islet of Motu Nui to await the first sooty tern egg of the season; the sponsor of the finder became tangata manu, the sacred birdman, for a year.</p></aside>
    </section>

